WEBVTT

00:00:01.483 --> 00:00:05.005
It seems today
 that all you see

00:00:05.030 --> 00:00:07.973
Is violence in movies
 and sex on TV

00:00:08.269 --> 00:00:12.012
But where are those
 good old-fashioned values

00:00:12.070 --> 00:00:14.996
On which we used to rely?

00:00:15.073 --> 00:00:18.332
Lucky there's a family guy

00:00:18.360 --> 00:00:21.803
Lucky there's a man who
 positively can do

00:00:21.880 --> 00:00:23.305
All the things that make us

00:00:23.381 --> 00:00:24.639
Laugh and cry

00:00:24.716 --> 00:00:30.437
He's... a...
 Fam... ily... Guy!

00:00:35.352 --> 00:00:37.119
Good morning.
I've come down to this floor

00:00:37.154 --> 00:00:38.678
because corporate
has figured out

00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:41.698
a new revenue stream:
giving tours of the brewery.

00:00:41.775 --> 00:00:44.083
And Peter, I've chosen you
for the job.

00:00:44.108 --> 00:00:45.132
That's great!

00:00:45.187 --> 00:00:47.379
Let me just call my old boss
and tell him to shove it.

00:00:50.042 --> 00:00:51.133
-Hello?
-Mr. Lloyd?

00:00:51.261 --> 00:00:53.428
This is Peter Griffin.
I quit.

00:00:53.453 --> 00:00:55.045
And I never sent in my pledge

00:00:55.121 --> 00:00:57.531
for your niece's
"Stand Up to Cancer" 5K.

00:00:58.099 --> 00:00:59.883
Hey, how's your niece,
by the way, she doing all right?

00:01:00.109 --> 00:01:01.685
-Very sick.
-Ah, terrific.

00:01:01.710 --> 00:01:03.226
Well, it was an honor
just to help.

00:01:03.279 --> 00:01:05.797
Now, here's everything
you'll need to be a tour guide--

00:01:05.874 --> 00:01:08.316
a blazer five people
hung themselves in,

00:01:08.393 --> 00:01:09.450
khakis that look dirty

00:01:09.528 --> 00:01:11.211
no matter how many times
you wash them,

00:01:11.236 --> 00:01:13.328
and a wet, brown banana
for lunch.

00:01:13.381 --> 00:01:15.474
Awesome. I love
telling people where to go,

00:01:15.550 --> 00:01:18.435
like when I cased that
McDonald's for The Hamburglar.

00:01:19.757 --> 00:01:21.273
There. At 11:45,

00:01:21.331 --> 00:01:23.498
they take the grease traps
out the back door.

00:01:23.725 --> 00:01:26.150
You sneak right in and take
all the hamburgers you want.

00:01:26.228 --> 00:01:27.561
-Robble, robble.
-Hey, man,

00:01:27.579 --> 00:01:29.412
I thought you just wanted
to score some hamburgers.

00:01:29.489 --> 00:01:31.226
These kids
don't have to die, man.

00:01:31.656 --> 00:01:33.567
Robble. Robble.

00:01:33.685 --> 00:01:36.586
Okay, take it easy. Be cool.
I don't want any robble.

00:01:39.729 --> 00:01:42.771
Hi, folks, I'm Peter Griffin,
and welcome to the brewery tour.

00:01:42.796 --> 00:01:43.935
All right, quick quiz--

00:01:44.012 --> 00:01:46.437
how many of you have heard
of beer before?

00:01:46.515 --> 00:01:48.181
Wow, half. That's pretty good.

00:01:48.410 --> 00:01:50.760
You can get a little closer,
gang, I don't bite.

00:01:50.785 --> 00:01:52.710
Too close!

00:01:53.613 --> 00:01:56.189
And we're proud to say
that Pawtucket Ale

00:01:56.191 --> 00:02:00.135
is responsible for 99%
of all DUIs in Rhode Island.

00:02:00.462 --> 00:02:01.338
Fascinating.

00:02:01.363 --> 00:02:02.637
Hey, shouldn't you be
doing the news?

00:02:02.714 --> 00:02:05.215
Oh, no, no, we're doing
a "Best of News Bloopers."

00:02:05.291 --> 00:02:06.475
Now, an update.
Apparently,

00:02:06.551 --> 00:02:08.702
the "Touth Sower"
has just collapsed.

00:02:08.704 --> 00:02:10.220
Tou-- "Touth Sower?"
What?

00:02:10.629 --> 00:02:12.147
"Touth--"
Okay, let's go again.

00:02:12.224 --> 00:02:14.632
I'm Tom Tower--
Holy crap.

00:02:14.710 --> 00:02:17.635
And now, please enjoy
a virtual reality experience

00:02:17.713 --> 00:02:19.713
about our founder,
Pawtucket Pat,

00:02:19.806 --> 00:02:22.465
in these headsets
that are definitely clean.

00:02:24.736 --> 00:02:27.237
Hi, I'm Casey Affleck,
aka Pawtucket Pat.

00:02:27.313 --> 00:02:28.813
I signed a contract to do this,

00:02:28.890 --> 00:02:30.073
then learned it filmed
the same day

00:02:30.149 --> 00:02:31.315
as Ben and J. Lo's wedding.

00:02:31.393 --> 00:02:33.409
Yet another great decision
by ol' Case.

00:02:33.811 --> 00:02:34.566
You'll cut that, right?

00:02:35.336 --> 00:02:39.026
Pawtucket Pat came to America
from England in 1771,

00:02:39.184 --> 00:02:40.350
looking for a better life.

00:02:40.426 --> 00:02:42.168
The seas were very rough.

00:02:42.345 --> 00:02:43.620
Pretty realistic, right?

00:02:46.724 --> 00:02:48.374
When Pat finally
reached the shore,

00:02:48.376 --> 00:02:50.562
the natives welcomed him
with a flurry of arrows

00:02:50.587 --> 00:02:51.871
to his colonial penis.

00:02:53.763 --> 00:02:56.716
Dear God,
why's we experiencing this?

00:02:56.718 --> 00:02:58.309
Please save your questions
for the end.

00:02:58.328 --> 00:03:02.664
In 1776, Pat refused to sign
the Declaration of Independence,

00:03:02.740 --> 00:03:05.032
saying the only thing
we need independence from

00:03:05.109 --> 00:03:06.501
is wives who won't let us drink.

00:03:06.578 --> 00:03:10.306
He left Philadelphia, uttering
several anti-Italian slurs

00:03:10.331 --> 00:03:11.989
on his way out of town,
all of which are true.

00:03:12.067 --> 00:03:14.158
Unfortunately, he didn't
realize Philadelphia is built

00:03:14.235 --> 00:03:16.511
on a platform 9,000 feet
in the air.

00:03:19.074 --> 00:03:20.849
Just take off your headsets.

00:03:22.858 --> 00:03:24.352
The fall proved to be fatal.

00:03:24.429 --> 00:03:26.170
Oh, yeah, and right before
 Pawtucket Pat died,

00:03:26.195 --> 00:03:27.528
he pooped his pants.

00:03:27.553 --> 00:03:29.870
We have pants available
in the gift shop.

00:03:33.617 --> 00:03:36.822
Okay, so now how many of you
know what beer is?

00:03:37.633 --> 00:03:39.150
So we did learn. Great.

00:03:39.325 --> 00:03:41.975
Okay, before we wrap it up,
any questions? Yes?

00:03:42.221 --> 00:03:45.306
How come Jeff Bezos wears
that big, weird cowboy hat

00:03:45.383 --> 00:03:46.883
when he rides his spaceship?

00:03:46.885 --> 00:03:48.809
I-I don't-- I don't know, Joe.

00:03:48.887 --> 00:03:51.571
Well, that's the tour, folks.
Please either tip me

00:03:51.596 --> 00:03:54.006
or shamefully avoid eye contact
on the way out.

00:03:54.675 --> 00:03:55.368
Coward.

00:03:55.612 --> 00:03:57.151
Coward. Coward.

00:03:57.450 --> 00:03:58.152
Coward.

00:03:58.171 --> 00:03:59.486
Friggin' cheapskate.

00:03:59.488 --> 00:04:00.839
Griffin, I'm glad I caught you.

00:04:00.915 --> 00:04:03.490
There's a VIP who wants
a tour of the brewery,

00:04:03.515 --> 00:04:05.532
and it's a bit
of a sensitive matter.

00:04:05.661 --> 00:04:07.904
-It's Brett Kavanaugh.
-Brett Ratner?

00:04:07.906 --> 00:04:10.831
-No. That's Brett Ratner.
-Brett Favre?

00:04:10.856 --> 00:04:12.705
No. That's a different
scumbag Brett.

00:04:12.812 --> 00:04:14.888
I'm talking about
the Supreme Court Justice.

00:04:14.913 --> 00:04:17.597
He'd like to take the tour,
and I don't want a spectacle.

00:04:17.673 --> 00:04:19.582
Sure. I don't got a problem
with anyone

00:04:19.584 --> 00:04:20.859
except
Jennifer Connelly's husband.

00:04:20.935 --> 00:04:24.028
- I love beer!
- That's him now.

00:04:26.805 --> 00:04:28.829
Hello, your judgesty,
Peter Griffin.

00:04:28.927 --> 00:04:31.664
Hey, just call me Brett.
All right, guys, skedaddle.

00:04:32.149 --> 00:04:33.315
I'm so pumped.

00:04:33.372 --> 00:04:35.206
I've toured every brewery
in the country

00:04:35.283 --> 00:04:37.093
except this one.
I love beer!

00:04:37.118 --> 00:04:38.746
Yeah, you've screamed
that twice now.

00:04:38.771 --> 00:04:41.287
I scream it all the time.
It's kind of how I got my job.

00:04:41.289 --> 00:04:43.231
-Me too.
-That's awesome.

00:04:43.458 --> 00:04:45.124
Tour time.
I love beer!

00:04:45.201 --> 00:04:47.886
Then you'll love
all the dull trivia behind it.

00:04:47.962 --> 00:04:50.613
Peter, I don't want
some normie dork tour.

00:04:51.056 --> 00:04:53.633
Look at us.
We're bloated kindred spirits.

00:04:53.972 --> 00:04:54.951
We even look alike.

00:04:54.953 --> 00:04:57.044
We're in love
with the same mistress, Peter.

00:04:57.122 --> 00:04:58.879
And you know everything
about her--

00:04:58.881 --> 00:05:01.733
her moods,
her little whims, her musk.

00:05:01.809 --> 00:05:03.735
Show me her world, Peter.

00:05:03.770 --> 00:05:06.613
Show me your... beer.

00:05:08.724 --> 00:05:11.576
Double keg stand.
Are there any chicks watching?

00:05:11.578 --> 00:05:13.803
No. Even better, just guys.

00:05:13.805 --> 00:05:15.154
One thing I do know--

00:05:15.231 --> 00:05:18.226
beer can only be drunk
in an upright body position.

00:05:18.526 --> 00:05:21.586
Uh, Keith? I'm gonna ask you
to turn around for a sec,

00:05:21.663 --> 00:05:24.163
and...
you're gonna feel pretty silly.

00:05:28.784 --> 00:05:32.348
Yes. We got to experience
what it's like to be beer.

00:05:32.373 --> 00:05:34.357
And we drank our own pee
in the can.

00:05:34.359 --> 00:05:36.359
-No, we didn't.
-Right. No, yeah, right.

00:05:36.361 --> 00:05:39.501
Hey, Brett, you're pretty cool
for a Supreme Court justice.

00:05:39.526 --> 00:05:41.878
That's all I want people to say.

00:05:44.485 --> 00:05:46.094
Last one in's a rotten egg!

00:05:46.170 --> 00:05:48.971
I will not be a rotten egg.

00:05:50.916 --> 00:05:54.435
Bro, let's see who can
get the reddest the fastest.

00:06:00.653 --> 00:06:04.104
I'm very drunk, Peter.
There are a lot of yous.

00:06:07.766 --> 00:06:09.342
I see a lot of yous.

00:06:09.441 --> 00:06:12.625
-Synchronized swimming?
-You know it.

00:07:09.612 --> 00:07:11.928
All people want to do
is scream at me

00:07:11.930 --> 00:07:14.301
in steakhouses
about women's bodies.

00:07:14.326 --> 00:07:16.175
Yeah.
My wife hates you,

00:07:16.177 --> 00:07:18.452
which kind of makes me
secretly like you.

00:07:21.273 --> 00:07:23.607
Hey, Brett?
Do you think that we'll still

00:07:23.684 --> 00:07:26.877
-be friends at college?
-I don't know, man.

00:07:35.076 --> 00:07:37.138
Oh, my God,
we were super drunk last night.

00:07:37.291 --> 00:07:39.420
Did I accidentally
kill Brett Kavanaugh?

00:07:40.408 --> 00:07:43.126
"Dear Peter, why did you
accidentally kill me?

00:07:43.204 --> 00:07:45.629
"Just kidding.
I don't want my life anymore.

00:07:45.706 --> 00:07:48.965
"You take it. Brett.
"PS, this is the first time

00:07:49.043 --> 00:07:50.967
"I've ever put clothes on anyone

00:07:50.992 --> 00:07:53.235
without their consent.
Ha, ha, ha."

00:07:54.224 --> 00:07:55.448
Justice Kavanaugh?

00:07:58.925 --> 00:07:59.783
It's him.

00:07:59.887 --> 00:08:01.645
Did you guys see that chick
in accounting?

00:08:01.722 --> 00:08:04.895
Boy, I'd like to hustle her
up some stairs against her will.

00:08:04.920 --> 00:08:06.983
-It's really him.
-All right, let's get him back

00:08:07.061 --> 00:08:09.178
to the Supreme Court
of the United States of America,

00:08:09.203 --> 00:08:11.230
where he serves
a lifetime appointment

00:08:11.232 --> 00:08:13.732
as one of only nine
Senate-confirmed justices.

00:08:13.734 --> 00:08:15.992
It's so cool that a guy
named Brett gets to decide

00:08:16.070 --> 00:08:17.386
if women can have abortions.

00:08:25.505 --> 00:08:28.897
So, anyone watch anything
interesting last night?

00:08:28.899 --> 00:08:31.324
Okay, I'm finally gonna
 say something.

00:08:31.418 --> 00:08:33.569
Or would it be weird,
 after being here 30 years,

00:08:33.571 --> 00:08:35.765
if the first thing I say is,
 "I like Shark Tank"?

00:08:35.947 --> 00:08:37.797
You can do this, Clarence.
 Here goes.

00:08:40.130 --> 00:08:42.538
There he is.
Hey, Kavanaugh.

00:08:42.563 --> 00:08:43.821
Sorry I'm late.
The steps outside

00:08:43.898 --> 00:08:45.381
are perfect for a slinky.

00:08:45.562 --> 00:08:48.190
Ah, I love
your refreshing honesty, Brett.

00:08:48.386 --> 00:08:49.976
Dears, can I get
a cup of coffee?

00:08:50.204 --> 00:08:52.980
Brett, we're Justices
Sotomayor and Barrett.

00:08:53.277 --> 00:08:54.148
Right, sorry.

00:08:54.225 --> 00:08:55.374
Hon, coffee?

00:08:55.376 --> 00:08:57.392
No, I'm Justice
Ketanji Brown Jackson.

00:08:57.469 --> 00:08:59.469
Yes, and I will definitely
remember your name

00:08:59.547 --> 00:09:01.955
and not butcher it
relentlessly going forward.

00:09:02.001 --> 00:09:03.667
-Toots, coffee?
-Stick it, Brett.

00:09:03.692 --> 00:09:06.877
I'm Justice Elena Kagan.
Ha-cha-cha.

00:09:07.145 --> 00:09:10.739
Okay, ready
for our morning introduction?

00:09:16.230 --> 00:09:18.564
Gathered together
 from Harvard and Yale--

00:09:18.566 --> 00:09:20.508
except the last lady
 Trump appointed--

00:09:20.584 --> 00:09:24.428
are the most boring forces
 of good ever assembled.

00:09:31.523 --> 00:09:32.980
John Roberts.

00:09:37.492 --> 00:09:40.069
Clarence Thomas
 and Samuel Alito.

00:09:47.170 --> 00:09:48.762
Elena Kagan.

00:09:52.024 --> 00:09:53.932
Get a visible car, bitch.

00:09:53.934 --> 00:09:57.694
Sonya Sotomayor
 is Aquaman in this, I guess.

00:09:57.981 --> 00:10:00.881
And the Wonder Twins,
 Barrett and Brown Jackson.

00:10:00.958 --> 00:10:02.550
We hate each other, though.

00:10:02.626 --> 00:10:04.701
With their space monkey,
 Kavanaugh.

00:10:04.703 --> 00:10:06.870
It's me, Peter.

00:10:08.115 --> 00:10:09.539
They're trying not to die

00:10:09.617 --> 00:10:11.967
until someone
 from their party is presiden.

00:10:12.316 --> 00:10:14.407
These are the Supreme Friends.

00:10:16.581 --> 00:10:18.507
All right, let's pick a case.

00:10:18.583 --> 00:10:21.602
We've got a bakery that won't
bake a cake for a gay wedding,

00:10:21.678 --> 00:10:24.513
a bakery that won't bake a cake
for a trans anniversary,

00:10:24.589 --> 00:10:27.499
a bakery that won't bake a cake
for a dog's birthday--

00:10:27.501 --> 00:10:29.574
Is it just all people
mad about cakes?

00:10:29.730 --> 00:10:31.427
It's mostly cakes, yes.

00:10:31.505 --> 00:10:33.064
Although there is this case,

00:10:33.089 --> 00:10:35.664
Hometown Buffet
 v. Peter Griffin.

00:10:35.693 --> 00:10:38.835
If the steaming hot dog water
is on the buffet table,

00:10:38.860 --> 00:10:40.562
it is part of the buffet.

00:10:44.156 --> 00:10:45.309
What'll it be, fellas?

00:10:45.436 --> 00:10:48.270
-Three beers.
-Sorry, can't. We're all out.

00:10:48.346 --> 00:10:50.088
What? How is that possible?

00:10:50.107 --> 00:10:52.282
"The Kav" drank it all.

00:10:54.221 --> 00:10:56.094
Ugh. Brett Kavanaugh.

00:10:56.096 --> 00:10:58.622
-I hate that guy.
-Me too.

00:11:00.211 --> 00:11:02.970
'Sup, I'm the Kav.
Mind if I sit down?

00:11:02.995 --> 00:11:05.787
-Kind of.
-Come on, I know my reputation,

00:11:05.812 --> 00:11:07.245
but can't we have one beer?

00:11:08.240 --> 00:11:10.008
Fine. One beer.

00:11:12.888 --> 00:11:15.556
-You guys play golf?
-Occasionally.

00:11:15.632 --> 00:11:17.040
You ever hit the ball
and it doesn't go

00:11:17.065 --> 00:11:18.299
where you thought it would?

00:11:18.378 --> 00:11:19.803
Sometimes.

00:11:19.828 --> 00:11:22.212
You ever putt
and it just, like, misses?

00:11:22.231 --> 00:11:24.456
Yeah, I've missed a putt or two.

00:11:24.458 --> 00:11:26.233
You ever get stuck
in a sand trap

00:11:26.310 --> 00:11:27.995
and you can't stop crying
'cause deep down

00:11:28.020 --> 00:11:29.499
you know your dad hates you?

00:11:29.947 --> 00:11:32.264
Brett Kavanaugh,
you're all right.

00:11:32.266 --> 00:11:34.421
Guys, we got to party together.

00:11:34.446 --> 00:11:36.526
This weekend?
Squee's mom's beach house?

00:11:36.604 --> 00:11:38.481
-Sounds epic.
-Party at the shore.

00:11:38.506 --> 00:11:40.697
What's the stair
situation there?

00:11:40.775 --> 00:11:42.518
There's a flight of stairs
to get in.

00:11:42.543 --> 00:11:45.618
Okay, we should probably
Airbnb another place.

00:11:45.696 --> 00:11:47.287
-Still in.
-100% in.

00:11:47.364 --> 00:11:50.140
Well, we can figure that out
later as a group.

00:11:53.053 --> 00:11:54.460
Therefore, in order to qualify

00:11:54.538 --> 00:11:58.874
for a hardship exemption
under Section 7545-09BI--

00:11:58.876 --> 00:12:02.194
Guys, I think I have a way
to make this more interesting.

00:12:04.786 --> 00:12:07.873
- With regard to the claim
of forum non conveniens--
- Boo!

00:12:08.052 --> 00:12:09.493
We're not turning for that.

00:12:11.967 --> 00:12:14.225
Tastes like strawberries

00:12:14.558 --> 00:12:17.209
On a summer evening

00:12:18.424 --> 00:12:21.534
And it sounds
 just like a song

00:12:22.155 --> 00:12:24.543
I want more berries

00:12:24.724 --> 00:12:26.971
And that summer feeling

00:12:28.595 --> 00:12:31.423
It's so wonderful and warm

00:12:31.499 --> 00:12:34.184
Watermelon sugar high

00:12:34.261 --> 00:12:36.687
Watermelon sugar
 high

00:12:36.763 --> 00:12:39.097
Watermelon sugar high

00:12:39.174 --> 00:12:41.500
Watermelon sugar
 high.

00:12:41.929 --> 00:12:43.935
That was a great idea,
everybody.

00:12:44.012 --> 00:12:45.178
Let's take lunch.

00:12:45.250 --> 00:12:47.900
Hey, how about today
we eat at the Mall?

00:12:47.925 --> 00:12:49.424
Okay, Clarence,

00:12:49.426 --> 00:12:51.109
there's never gonna be
 a better setup to make

00:12:51.186 --> 00:12:53.445
your "Supreme Food Court" joke.
 Here goes.

00:12:53.656 --> 00:12:55.038
Hey, if we're going to the Mall,

00:12:55.115 --> 00:12:57.966
how about we eat
at the Supreme Food Court?

00:13:00.570 --> 00:13:02.454
It's like he heard my thought.

00:13:02.530 --> 00:13:05.198
That's right, Clarence.
 I can hear thoughts.

00:13:05.275 --> 00:13:07.459
But it only works
 on white-haired black guys.

00:13:07.535 --> 00:13:09.127
Do you want to know
 how Danny Glover

00:13:09.204 --> 00:13:11.471
really felt about Mel Gibson?

00:13:19.757 --> 00:13:22.248
-Lois, what's going on with--
 -My hair? My beard?

00:13:22.273 --> 00:13:24.987
Because you took a lifetime
 appointment in Washington,

00:13:25.012 --> 00:13:26.453
I'm doing everything.

00:13:26.530 --> 00:13:29.514
Sorry I haven't had
 a second to wax and dye mysel.

00:13:29.516 --> 00:13:31.329
Well, that'll make him
 want to come back.

00:13:31.354 --> 00:13:33.460
Lois, this is the first time
in our marriage

